                "post_type": "post",
                "quote_count": 13,
                "quoted_status_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 47,
                "retweet_count": 312,
                "source": "Buffer",
                "text": "Since the Big Mess of a Budget Bill did not pass on Friday, we members of the Budget committee were called into a meeting to vote at 10p this evening.\n\nRepublicans literally rushed to jam through a bill that makes the largest cuts to Medicaid and food assistance in American history\u2014ripping away lifelines that tens of millions of Americans rely on.\n\nAnd, do not be fooled\u2014the \u201cno\u201d votes from certain Republicans on Friday were because the cuts were not fast or deep enough. In the back room, Republicans agreed to deeper and especially faster cuts to programs. \n\nMy Democratic colleagues and I are still here, though. And, we will still fight to protect care, lower costs, and invest in working families. \n\ud83d\udcaf\ud83d\udcaa\ud83c\udffd\ud83d\ude4f\ud83c\udffd",
